Code disclosure: scripts/tally.py reads one user-named UTF-8 text file and prints
section-level judicial speaking turns and approximate whitespace-delimited word
counts. It uses the Python standard library only. It makes no network calls,
writes no files, starts no child processes, and performs no dynamic code evaluation.
It requires official-style headings and manual verification against the transcript.

